@page "/when-the-storm-hits"
<PageTitle>When the storm hits · Tangent Atlas</PageTitle>

<div class="ta-container ta-page">
    <h1 class="ta-page-headline">When the storm hits</h1>
    <p class="ta-page-sub">You decided in March. In October, your rules respond. Discipline is deciding calmly, ahead of time, what happens to every dollar. Here is one example of what that looks like.</p>

    <div class="ta-storm">
        <div class="ta-storm-rules">
            <div class="ta-eyebrow ta-eyebrow-muted">Your rules, set in March</div>
            <ul>
                <li>Keep my investments 70% stocks, 30% bonds and cash</li>
                <li>Never sell my favorite stocks</li>
                <li>Keep checking between $5,000 and $10,000</li>
                <li>Nothing trades until I approve it</li>
            </ul>
        </div>
        <ol class="ta-storm-steps">
            <li><span class="ta-storm-dot">1</span><span><strong>Stocks fall 20%.</strong> Your mix drifts from 70% stocks to 65%.</span></li>
            <li><span class="ta-storm-dot">2</span><span><strong>Atlas checks every account against your rules.</strong> Checking is inside its band; your favorites are off limits.</span></li>
            <li><span class="ta-storm-dot">3</span><span><strong>It shows you the plan.</strong> Move $12,600 from bonds and cash back into stocks to return to 70%, without touching your favorites.</span></li>
            <li><span class="ta-storm-dot">4</span><span><strong>You approve.</strong> The orders go to your own broker, and you get a record of what was done and why.</span></li>
        </ol>
    </div>
    <p class="ta-caption">An illustration of rules a customer might set, with round numbers. Not a forecast or a recommendation: you choose the rules.</p>
</div>
